    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266">

                <pb facs="0364" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862i.01/46a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-06T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>442. For the Ambassador, for transmission to the Foreign Office.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>I have transmitted to my Government your memorandum of November 19th<anchor
                            n="15" xml:id="d266-f1"/> in reply to the memorandum submitted by me on
                        the 12th of November regarding the island of Yap, to which my Government has
                        directed me to reply as follows:</p>
                    <pb facs="0365" n="269" xml:id="pg269"/>
                    <p>[Here follows, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, the
                        communication to the British Government contained in telegram no. 1199,
                        December 4, 1920, to the Ambassador in Great Britain, beginning with the
                        words “There would appear.” In the paragraph beginning “I am directed” the
                        words “for such purposes” are inserted after the words “free and unhampered
                        use”.]</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d266-f1" n="15" xml:id="d266-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 598, Nov. 19, from the Chargé in Japan, <ref target="#pg264">p.
                        264</ref>.</p>
            </note>
